From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kanadaj <kanadaj@royalroad.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:52:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Make the Pipelines namespaces configurable at build time

The plugin hard-codes openshift-pipelines, the namespace the OpenShift
Pipelines operator installs into. Clusters that install Tekton from the
upstream release YAMLs keep their shared Task library and Pipelines-as-Code
elsewhere, so the pipeline builder offered no cluster resolver Tasks and
the PaC pages looked in the wrong namespace.

PIPELINE_NAMESPACE (PaC secret and configuration) and
CLUSTER_RESOLVER_TASK_NAMESPACE (Tasks the builder offers through the
cluster resolver, and the default namespace of cluster resolver
references without one) can now be set at build time. Both default to
openshift-pipelines, so OpenShift builds are unchanged.
---
 src/components/pipeline-builder/hooks.ts  |  4 ++--
 src/components/pipeline-builder/utils.ts  |  8 ++++----
 src/components/pipelines-details/utils.ts |  6 +++---
 src/consts.ts                             | 10 +++++++++-
 webpack.config.ts                         | 11 ++++++++++-
 5 files changed, 28 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

